From: Hazel Smith <hazel@hazelesque.uk>
Subject: mimalloc.h: allow caller to override mi_decl_export under MI_LIBC_BUILD

In the upstream main/musl build, mimalloc is compiled with
MI_LIBC_BUILD=1, which makes mimalloc.h define mi_decl_export
unconditionally as `static`.  This collapses the entire mimalloc
public API (mi_malloc, mi_stats_print_out, mi_collect, etc.) to
file-static visibility, so even nm on the resulting .o sees them
as lowercase 't' (local) — they cannot be exported from
libc.so no matter how the link is configured.

For the hazelesque/musl-mimalloc-introspectable variant we want
to expose mimalloc's introspection API as proper dynamic symbols.
Making the `static` definition `#ifndef`-guarded lets the variant's
mimalloc.c shim predefine `mi_decl_export` to
`__attribute__((visibility("default")))` before the include cascade
reaches mimalloc.h.

Behaviour for existing builds (main/musl) is unchanged: they don't
predefine mi_decl_export, so the `static` define still wins.

This patch is hazelesque-only — main/musl/ does not need it.

diff --git a/mimalloc/include/mimalloc.h b/mimalloc/include/mimalloc.h
--- a/mimalloc/include/mimalloc.h
+++ b/mimalloc/include/mimalloc.h
@@ -60,8 +60,11 @@
   #define mi_attr_alloc_size2(s1,s2)
   #define mi_attr_alloc_align(p)
 #elif defined(__GNUC__)                 // includes clang and icc
-  #ifdef MI_LIBC_BUILD
+  #if defined(MI_LIBC_BUILD) && !defined(mi_decl_export)
     #define mi_decl_export static
+  #elif defined(MI_LIBC_BUILD)
+    /* caller predefined mi_decl_export — keep their definition.
+       Used by hazelesque/musl-mimalloc-introspectable. */
   #elif defined(MI_SHARED_LIB) && defined(MI_SHARED_LIB_EXPORT)
     #define mi_decl_export              __attribute__((visibility("default")))
   #else
